## Slot vocabulary ({{slot-count}} slots inherited or declared)

Artifact memorials inherit the full `:mm/Memory` slot vocabulary — identity (name / description / scope), provenance (created / last-touched / last-reviewed / created-by / importance), typed-edge predicates (cites / related / refines / evidences / motivated-by / supersedes / superseded-by / ...), structural fields (body-raw / first-section / links / frontmatter / tags / themes), and origin tracking (bootstrap-source / bootstrap-override).

Concrete subtypes layer their own type-specific slots on top — e.g., `:mm.decision/alternatives` for Decision, `:mm.plan/stage` + `:mm.plan/status` for Plan.

{{slot-table}}

## Composition with other classes

- **`:mm/Section`** — body decomposition.  Each H2+ heading becomes an addressable section entity for fine-grained cross-reference.
- **`:mm/Tag`** — classification.  Tags can be free-text (informal) or canonical (controlled-vocabulary via `:mm/ConceptScheme`).
- **`:mm/Link`** — markdown-link extraction.  Body links become first-class entities for backlink queries.
- **`:mm/Frontmatter`** — long-tail extra frontmatter keys not declared on the concrete subtype.

